A: Figure 25: Unfolded (Eavail , W ) cross section versus the four-generator band (GENIE CV, GENIE+MEC, NuWro, GiBUU; GENIE and NuWro flux-corrected, §7.6). Every generator lies below the data in the high-W , high-Eavail corner — GENIE and NuWro by about their overall normalization shortfall, GiBUU by more; adding 2p2h leaves the corner unchanged because 2p2h populates low W . MINERvA shallow-inelastic neutrino and antineutrino measurements also report shape and normalization disagreements with generators [49]. They motivate tests across the resonance–DIS
B: FIG. 9. Absolutely normalized ratios of data, GENIE 2.8.4, NuWro, and GiBUU to MnvGENIE v1 for pT and p|| . The transverse momentum projection shows tension between all models and data in the 0.55 < pT < 1.50 GeV range, with the highest pT bin modeled the best. In longitudinal momentum, all models underpredict the cross section, with the most significant discrepancy of a 20 to 40% normalization difference occurring with GiBUU.
